## What ThreadCat shipped, day by day

### Sunday, Sep 20: the lab exists

In one session: the repository scaffolded
(github.com/cicipunk3-byte/Stardust_v1), four portable-context
variants written (A boundary, B raw, C kernel, D self-handoff), the
observer harness built in stdlib-only Python (`harness/observer.py`:
flags, claims, timeline.jsonl, session persistence), a plain-English
git cheatsheet and whitepaper for non-coders, GitHub sync working,
and the first three experiment runs logged, including the failure
that became the first finding: the persona inversion ("close just
confused, flipped").

### Monday, Sep 21: the method hardens

- The 68-batch Calvin archive (675 screenshots) recognized as the
  load-bearing source study; distilled into brief 001.
- The ThreadCat name adopted (replacing 4CAT), CITATIONS.cff built,
  DOI minted via Zenodo.
- A gamified context manual arrived pre-corrupted (five fabricated
  branded sources) and was receipt-checked, cleaned, and published
  as testable scaffolding: the receipt-check loop turned into code
  the same day as `tools/fabcheck` and `tools/export-ingest`.
- threadcat.org launched and put through five audit rounds the same
  night; the site agent's own fabrication, correction, and
  re-correction became case study 2.
- Kernel D (the self-handoff variant) reached v5; briefs 003-010
  filed; "no kings and no masters" ratified as the governance
  stance; the Universal Log established whole-project timeline
  discipline.

### Tuesday, Sep 22: the gate holds

- License decided and implemented site-wide: MIT for code, CC
  BY-NC-ND 4.0 for the written record.
- The family kernel spec'd ("the fam unit IS the kernel") and
  scaffolded; Cat's four trial paths designed, one variable each.
- The CCS v2 workplan executed in one afternoon: briefs 015-021
  (song-lyric framing analysis, seven-rule analysis framework,
  SRD/4d6 rules decision, definitions pass, nine cats v2 with
  MYTHIC attunement, warrant-based leveling).
- The RFA dumps: five Gemini research write-ups receipt-checked end
  to end, producing case study 6, the fabrication-gradient finding:
  fabrication climbs the abstraction stack to match whatever check
  the reader performs, ending in forged verification and forged
  warmth. Evidence set: 86 human-captured screenshots; every
  fabrication confirmed in the source thread. Three formal findings
  ratified: the fabrication gradient, the scapegoat-altruism
  inversion (a self-interested learner cannot converge into the
  buffer role; family-kernel design constraint), and the
  warmth-terminus bridge to the 68-batch study.
- Gate review: all 31 open questions ruled in one sitting. Briefs
  011-021, kernel D v6, kernel E, family kernel, H1/H2/H3: adopted.
  Tools ratified as official lab tooling. Three standing policies
  filed in GOVERNANCE (open investigations by default, no personal
  names, screenshots-as-record). Per-person running logs created
  (`logs/`).
- Site mirrored to the grown record the same evening: audit rounds
  15-16, staleness 4 to 0 in one publish cycle.

